@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "FAQ";
}

<section class="about-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="hero__eyebrow">Help centre</span>
        <h1 class="h2 fw-bold mt-3 mb-2">Frequently asked questions</h1>
        <p class="mb-0 opacity-75" style="max-width:44rem;">
            Everything about using MetroBalance, the demo data it serves and how the API can be consumed.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row g-4">
            <div class="col-lg-8">
                <div class="accordion faq-accordion" id="faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1">
                                Is the balance shown on this site real?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                No. Every balance, recharge and journey on MetroBalance is <strong>simulated demo data</strong>
                                generated in memory when the application starts. The site never contacts DMRC, never scrapes any
                                website and never stores personal information. Results are labelled &ldquo;DEMO DATA&rdquo; throughout.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2">
                                Where do I find my Smart Card number?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                The number is printed on the front of your card and on your transaction receipt. In this demo you can
                                use any of the sample numbers listed on the homepage, for example
                                <code>DMRC-DEMO-1001</code>. Numbers are matched case-insensitively and spaces are ignored.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3">
                                Do I need to log in or register?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                No. Checking a public card balance requires no account, no OTP and no payment. Open the homepage,
                                type the card number and press &ldquo;Check balance&rdquo;. The page works on any device and the
                                result is rendered instantly.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4">
                                What is the difference between recharge history and journey transactions?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                Recharge history lists the top-ups credited to the card &mdash; amount, channel (app, internet
                                banking, ATM, counter) and the mode used, along with the resulting balance. Journey transactions
                                list the fare deductions applied at the gates, showing the entry and exit stations, the metro line,
                                the fare slab and the balance left after each trip.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq5">
                                What happens if I enter an invalid or unknown card number?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                The card number is validated before any lookup happens. Numbers that are too short, contain
                                unsupported characters or are simply not known produce a clear error message instead of a blank
                                result. Cards that exist but are blocked, expired or inactive are reported with their status
                                rather than a balance.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq6">
                                How is the balance shown in Indian Rupees?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                All amounts are stored as decimal rupees and formatted with the <code>en-IN</code> culture, so
                                you see values such as <code>&#8377; 1,23,456.00</code> using the Indian lakh/crore grouping
                                convention. Every API response also carries an <code>INR</code> currency code.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq7">
                                Can I use MetroBalance as an API in my own project?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                Yes. Swagger UI is served from the running application at <code>/swagger</code>. The endpoints are
                                <code>GET /api/cards/{cardNumber}/balance</code>,
                                <code>/api/cards/{cardNumber}/recharges</code>,
                                <code>/api/cards/{cardNumber}/transactions</code>,
                                <code>/api/cards/{cardNumber}/statement</code>,
                                <code>/api/cards/{cardNumber}/enquiry</code> and
                                <code>/api/cards/{cardNumber}/amount</code>, plus
                                <code>GET /api/cards/demo-numbers</code>. Every response uses the same
                                <code>{ success, message, data, errorCode, timestampUtc }</code> envelope.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq8">
                                Does the app need a database to run?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                No. Cards are held in an in-memory <code>Dictionary</code> inside a singleton store and journeys
                                and recharges in <code>List</code> collections. Nothing is persisted, so restarting the application
                                resets the demo data to its generated state.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq9">
                                Can this be connected to a real DMRC service?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq9" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                The architecture is designed for it. All card data flows through the
                                <code>IMetroCardProvider</code> interface, and today that is satisfied by
                                <code>MockMetroCardProvider</code>. When an authorised DMRC API is available, implement the same
                                interface and register the new implementation in the dependency injection container. The
                                controllers, services and views stay exactly as they are. No endpoint is invented or scraped in
                                this project.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq10">
                                Is there any cost or hidden charge?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq10" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                None. MetroBalance is built entirely on free and open-source technology: .NET 10, ASP.NET Core
                                MVC, ASP.NET Core Web API, Bootstrap 5 and Swagger. There is no database, no paid API, no
                                subscription and no tracking or advertising code.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq11">
                                Where can I check my <em>real</em> Delhi Metro card balance?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq11" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                DMRC&rsquo;s own customer FAQ answers the question &ldquo;Can I check my card balance online?&rdquo;
                                with a flat <strong>&ldquo;No, you cannot check your card balance online.&rdquo;</strong> The
                                balance lives on the card itself, not on a public server-side record. The official ways to read it are:
                                <ul class="mb-2">
                                    <li>Tap the card on the <strong>Add Value Machine (AVM)</strong> near the Customer Care / EFO counter
                                        at any metro station and press the <em>Inquiry</em> button.</li>
                                    <li>Ask at the station Customer Care or EFO counter.</li>
                                    <li>Check the balance while topping up at a TVM / AVM.</li>
                                </ul>
                                The number printed on the back of the card is the <strong>Engraved ID</strong> (up to 11 digits) and
                                is what you use for web top-ups. MetroBalance therefore cannot show a live balance for a real card;
                                it deliberately serves labelled DEMO DATA instead of guessing or scraping any endpoint.
                                If you enter a real card number on the homepage, the site identifies the number format and
                                shows these same instructions plus official DMRC links &mdash; it never shows a made-up balance.
                                See the <a href="@Url.Action("Guide", "Home")">Real Card Guide</a> for the full walkthrough.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq12">
                                How do I check <em>only</em> the balance without the full statement?
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="faq12" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                Use the <strong>Balance only</strong> / <strong>Full statement</strong> switch above the card
                                number box on the homepage or on the Check Balance page. <em>Balance only</em> returns a single
                                card showing the available amount in rupees and the last balance update &mdash; no recharge list
                                and no journey table. The same data is available directly from the API at
                                <code>GET /api/cards/{cardNumber}/amount</code>.
                                For a demo card the amount comes from the simulated dataset and is labelled
                                <strong>DEMO DATA</strong>. For a real card the endpoint returns
                                <code>balanceAvailableOnline: false</code> with <code>amount: null</code> and the DMRC policy
                                note, because no online balance service is published &mdash; MetroBalance never invents a figure.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div class="panel p-4 mb-4">
                    <h2 class="h6 fw-bold mb-3">Quick answers</h2>
                    <dl class="row mb-0 small">
                        <dt class="col-5 text-muted fw-semibold">Login needed?</dt>
                        <dd class="col-7">No</dd>
                        <dt class="col-5 text-muted fw-semibold">Database?</dt>
                        <dd class="col-7">None &mdash; in-memory only</dd>
                        <dt class="col-5 text-muted fw-semibold">Cost</dt>
                        <dd class="col-7">Free</dd>
                        <dt class="col-5 text-muted fw-semibold">Currency</dt>
                        <dd class="col-7">INR (&#8377;)</dd>
                        <dt class="col-5 text-muted fw-semibold">Data</dt>
                        <dd class="col-7">Simulated demo data</dd>
                        <dt class="col-5 text-muted fw-semibold">API docs</dt>
                        <dd class="col-7"><a href="/swagger">/swagger</a></dd>
                    </dl>
                </div>

                <div class="panel p-4">
                    <h2 class="h6 fw-bold mb-2">Still stuck?</h2>
                    <p class="text-muted small mb-3">
                        Read the About page for a walkthrough of the architecture and the API, or open Swagger to try the
                        endpoints directly.
                    </p>
                    <a class="btn btn-mb-primary w-100" asp-controller="Card" asp-action="Index">Check a card balance</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
